Frontend: SDD

Purpose:
  Frontend technology catalog with framework options, selection criteria,
  and compatibility rules. Root stack/ defines reusable frontend knowledge;
  projects/{project_name}/stack/ stores the selected frontend for the current project.

Catalog:
  React:
    Type: Library
    Pros:
      - Largest ecosystem
      - Excellent community support
      - Flexible architecture
      - Strong hiring pool
    Cons:
      - Steep learning curve
      - Multiple state management options
      - Frequent ecosystem changes
    BestFor:
      - Complex SPAs
      - Large teams
      - Long-term projects
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple static sites (prefer vanilla/Svelte)
      - SEO-critical without SSR
    Frameworks:
      - Next.js: SSR, SSG, App Router
      - Remix: Nested routes, web standards
      - Vite + React: Fast development
    Performance:
      - Excellent with optimization
      - Virtual DOM overhead
    Ecosystem:
      - Very large
    Hiring:
      - Widely available

  Vue:
    Type: Framework
    Pros:
      - Gentle learning curve
      - Excellent documentation
      - Flexible architecture
      - Built-in state management
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem than React
      - Less enterprise adoption
    BestFor:
      - Medium complexity SPAs
      - Smaller teams
      - Rapid prototyping
    AvoidWhen:
      - Very large enterprise apps
      - Teams with React experience
    Frameworks:
      - Nuxt: SSR, SSG, auto-routing
      - Vite + Vue: Fast development
    Performance:
      - Excellent
    Ecosystem:
      - Moderate
    Hiring:
      - Moderate availability

  Angular:
    Type: Framework
    Pros:
      - Complete framework
      - Strong typing with TypeScript
      - Enterprise support
      - Built-in everything
    Cons:
      - Steep learning curve
      - Verbose
      - Heavy bundle size
    BestFor:
      - Enterprise applications
      - Large teams
      - Long-term maintenance
    AvoidWhen:
      - Rapid prototyping
      - Small teams
    Frameworks:
      - Standalone Angular
    Performance:
      - Good with optimization
    Ecosystem:
      - Mature
    Hiring:
      - Moderate availability

  Svelte:
    Type: Compiler
    Pros:
      - No virtual DOM
      - Minimal bundle size
      - Simple syntax
      - Fast development
    Cons:
      - Smaller ecosystem
      - Less mature tooling
      - Smaller hiring pool
    BestFor:
      - Performance-critical SPAs
      - Small to medium apps
      - Static sites
    AvoidWhen:
      - Very complex apps
      - Large teams needing structure
    Frameworks:
      - SvelteKit: SSR, SSG
    Performance:
      - Excellent
    Ecosystem:
      - Growing
    Hiring:
      - Limited availability

SelectionRules:
  - RequirementFit: project complexity and requirements
  - TeamFit: existing team expertise MUST be considered
  - Ecosystem: library maturity and community support
  - Performance: page load and interaction requirements
  - SEO: SSR/SSG requirements for content pages
  - Hiring: availability of skilled developers
  - Maintenance: long-term maintenance burden

TechnologyScore:
  RequirementFit: 0-25
  TeamFit: 0-20
  Ecosystem: 0-15
  Performance: 0-10
  SEO: 0-10
  Hiring: 0-10
  Maintenance: 0-10

State: +
  